    "lawCode": "Add §49, Cor L",
    "lawSection": "Correction Law",
    "memo": "\n \nBILL NUMBER: S5468\n\nSPONSOR: PARKER\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the correction law, in relation to establishing a\ncommission on improving education in state prisons\n\n \nPURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL:\n\nThis bill would amend the correction law by adding a new section that\nestablishes a commission on improving prison education.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF SPECIFIC PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1 of adds a new section 49 to the correction law. This section\nstates that there is hereby established a commission on prison education\ncomprised of nine members who shall study and develop a Plan for improv-\ning education in the state prison system. The commission shall consider\nand investigate the following factors when determining education\nimprovements: the impact on inmate's employment opportunities upon\nrelease from prison, the impact on an inmate's reintegration into socie-\nty and the effectiveness in reducing recidivism.\n\nAppointments to the task force shall be made as follows: three by the\ngovernor; two by the speaker of the assembly; one by the minority leader\nof the assembly; two by the temporary president of the senate and one by\nthe minority leader of the senate.\n\nThe commission shall issue a report within ten months after the effec-\ntive date of this paragraph.\n\nSection 2 this act shall take effect immediately.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nRehabilitation of inmates at prisons is more than simple punishment; it\nshould involve a strong education curriculum to ensure that rehabili-\ntated inmates do not resort to crime when they are released.  Released\ninmates often have difficulty finding jobs as convicted felons. The lack\nof quality education in prisons helps contribute to the recidivism of\nsome inmates. This commission is charged with defining the skills that\nwill help inmates return to society as a more productive citizen.\n\n \nPRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\n2019-20: S.5002 - Referred to Crime Victims, Crime and Correction\n2017-18: S.2235 - REPORTED AND COMMITTED TO FINANCE\n2015-16: S.2520/A.5973 - Referred to Crime Victims, Crime, and\nCorrections\n2013-14: S.2782/A.1107 - Referred to Crime Victims, Crime, and\nCorrections\n2011-12: S.6702/A.2315 - Referred to Crime Victims, Crime, and\nCorrections\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nMinimal.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
